issing_values":"no"},{"name":" ","role":"","type":" ","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"}],"additional_info":{"summary":"1593 handwritten digits from around 80 persons were scanned, stretched in a rectangular box 16x16 in a gray scale of 256 values.Then each pixel of each image was scaled into a bolean (1/0) value using a fixed threshold.\r\n\r\nEach person wrote on a paper all the digits from 0 to 9, twice. The commitment was to write the digit the first time in the normal way (trying to write each digit accurately) and the second time in a fast way (with no accuracy). \r\n\r\nThe best validation protocol for this dataset seems to be a 5x2CV, 50% Tune (Train +Test) and completly blind 50% Validation","purpose":null,"funded_by":null,"instances_represent":null,"recommended_data_splits":null,"sensitive_data":null,"preprocessing_description":null,"variable_info":"This dataset consists of 1593 records (rows) and 256 attributes (columns).\r\n\r\nEach record represents a handwritten digit, orginally scanned with a resolution of 256 grays scale (28).\r\n\r\nEach pixel of the each original scanned image was first stretched,  and after scaled between 0 and 1 (setting to 0 every pixel whose value was under tha value 127 of the grey scale (127 included) and setting to 1 each pixel whose orinal value in the grey scale was over 127).\r\n\r\nFinally, each binary image was scaled again into a 16x16 square box (the final 256 binary attributes). ","citation":null}}}